<h2>Insurance setup: TWIA, flood, and certificates</h2>
<p>San Patricio County is inside the TWIA designated catastrophe area, so many Ingleside properties have wind and hail coverage through TWIA and other perils through a homeowners or commercial policy. Flood is separate: standard policies generally exclude it, and coverage comes from the NFIP or a private flood policy, usually after a 30-day waiting period. Bayfront and low-lying properties should review flood coverage before hurricane season.</p>
<p>TWIA claims generally must be filed within one year of the date of loss. For TWIA eligibility, structures built, altered, or repaired on or after January 1, 1988 need a windstorm certificate of compliance, and re-roofs and roof repairs fall under the TDI Windstorm Inspection Program. Since April 1, 2026, windstorm certificate applications must be certified to the 2024 IRC or 2024 IBC. City of Ingleside permit requirements are set locally; check with the city before work begins. Read more on <a href="/services/twia-windstorm-claims/">TWIA windstorm claims</a> and <a href="/windstorm-certificate-wpi-8-insurance-claims/">WPI-8 windstorm certificates</a>.</p>

<h2>What San Patricio County storm data shows</h2>
<p>NCEI's San Patricio County records give useful context for Ingleside owners. The county has 108 thunderstorm wind reports, with May the busiest month, 58 tornado reports, and 110 flash flood reports. In other words, Ingleside claims are not only about hurricanes. A spring squall line can do as much damage to a roof or a large oak as a tropical storm, and heavy rain can flood low streets with no named storm involved. Because flood exclusions apply to rising water regardless of the cause, owners in low areas should look at flood coverage even if they are not on the water.</p>
<p>Common Ingleside claim issues include trees falling on roofs and fences, wind-driven rain entering through damaged shingles or flashing, damaged metal roofs and outbuildings, and, for bayfront homes, separating wind damage from surge damage after a tropical system. Search your address in our <a href="/storm-lookup/">storm lookup tool</a> to see reports near you.</p>

<h2>Residential and commercial claims</h2>
<p>For homeowners, we document roof damage, interior water intrusion, and personal property, and we prepare an itemized estimate. For businesses, we look at building damage, equipment, signage, and business income coverage where it exists; see our <a href="/services/commercial-property-claims/">commercial property claims</a> page. If an insurer has already paid less than the repair cost, our <a href="/services/underpaid-insurance-claims/">underpaid claims</a> and <a href="/services/insurance-appraisal/">insurance appraisal</a> pages explain the options a policy may provide.</p>
